# PhytoScope citation metadata (CFF 1.2.0)
#
# DOI / ORCID / affiliation placeholders below are UNFILLED and intentionally kept
# as comments so this file stays valid Citation File Format. Zenodo software and
# dataset deposits have NOT been created or published yet — DOI 未取得.
# After the maintainer publishes the two Zenodo deposits, replace the placeholders
# with real values (待 Zenodo 发布后回填). Central registry:
#   docs/fcs-zenodo-handoff.md
#
# Placeholders (all unfilled, none substituted with a guessed real value):
#   {{SOFTWARE_DOI}}   software deposit DOI (Zenodo Deposit A)
#   {{DATA_DOI}}       dataset deposit DOI (Zenodo Deposit B)
#   {{PAPER_DOI}}      paper DOI (after FCS publication)
#   {{ORCID}}          author ORCID iD
#   {{AFFILIATION}}    author affiliation
#
# Template lines to activate after publication (do not fill in now):
#   doi: "{{SOFTWARE_DOI}}"
#   identifiers:
#     - type: doi
#       value: "{{DATA_DOI}}"
#       description: "Reference-data deposit (Zenodo), unfilled until published"

cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use PhytoScope, please cite this software (version 0.3.0) and, where
  applicable, its reference-data deposit. Software DOI {{SOFTWARE_DOI}} and dataset
  DOI {{DATA_DOI}} are unfilled placeholders: the Zenodo deposits are pending and
  no DOI has been obtained. Replace them only after the maintainer publishes the
  deposits (待 Zenodo 发布后回填); see docs/fcs-zenodo-handoff.md and CITATION.cff.
title: "PhytoScope: portable local queries of plant genome data"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Song
    given-names: X
    # orcid: "{{ORCID}}"        # unfilled — 待 Zenodo 发布后回填
    # affiliation: "{{AFFILIATION}}"  # unfilled — 待 Zenodo 发布后回填
  - family-names: Chen
    given-names: P
  - family-names: Liang
    given-names: F
version: 0.3.0
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/omixcore/phytoscope"
url: "https://gitee.com/omixcore/phytoscope"
keywords:
  - plant genome
  - genome browser
  - JavaFX
  - reproducibility
  - GFF3
abstract: >-
  PhytoScope is a locally running JavaFX desktop browser for plant gene
  structures, providing a species-independent import-browse-query-compare-export
  pipeline with SHA-256 provenance and portable projects. Software and data
  Zenodo DOIs ({{SOFTWARE_DOI}} / {{DATA_DOI}}) are not yet obtained; the GitHub
  Release v0.3.0 is published (2026-11-14), and v0.2.0 remains as a historical
  archive.
